IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tcta-types`

-- Taxation (Cross-border Trade) Act 2018 (UK) — GOALS 1-3: LIABILITY, PERSONS
-- LIABLE, AMOUNT AND NOTIFICATION.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2018-22.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — liability to import duty`

DECLARE `Rate basis` IS ONE OF
    `the applicable rate`
    `the reduced rate for the procedure`
    `the normal rate, less any earlier liability`

DECLARE `Liability` HAS
    `incurred on`                                       IS A DATE
    `basis`                                             IS A `Rate basis`

-- s 4(1): free circulation — at acceptance. (2)-(3): storage, transit and
-- inward processing — none, unless the declaration was unentitled (at the
-- time it was made) or a requirement is breached (when first breached).
-- (4): authorised use or temporary admission — at acceptance, at the reduced
-- rate if entitled and the normal rate if not; and a further liability at a
-- breach at the normal rate less the earlier liability. s 5(2): goods not
-- presented or not declared — when they become liable to forfeiture. s 2(1):
-- domestic goods are not chargeable.
@ref ss 2(1), 4(1)-(4), 5(2)
@export The liabilities to import duty incurred under ss 4-5 of the Taxation (Cross-border Trade) Act 2018 (UK), each with its date and rate basis: none for domestic goods; at acceptance for the free-circulation procedure; for storage, transit or inward processing only at an unentitled declaration or the first breach; for authorised use or temporary admission at acceptance (reduced rate if entitled) and again at a breach (normal rate less the earlier liability); for goods not presented or declared, when they become liable to forfeiture. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN g IS A `Goods facts`  @desc Whether the goods are domestic, the procedure, entitlement, and the dates of declaration, acceptance, breach and forfeiture
GIVETH A LIST OF `Liability`
`the import duty liabilities for` g MEANS
    IF g's `domestic goods` THEN EMPTY
    ELSE CONSIDER g's `procedure`
         WHEN `free-circulation procedure` THEN atAcceptance `the applicable rate`
         WHEN `authorised use procedure` THEN specialUse
         WHEN `temporary admission procedure` THEN specialUse
         WHEN `not presented or not declared` THEN
             CONSIDER g's `liable to forfeiture on`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
             WHEN JUST d  THEN LIST (`Liability` OF d, `the applicable rate`)
         OTHERWISE
             IF   NOT (g's `entitled to make the declaration`)
             THEN LIST (`Liability` OF g's `declaration made on`, `the applicable rate`)
             ELSE CONSIDER g's `first breach on`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
                  WHEN JUST b  THEN LIST (`Liability` OF b, `the applicable rate`)
    WHERE
        GIVEN basis IS A `Rate basis`
        GIVETH A LIST OF `Liability`
        atAcceptance basis MEANS
            CONSIDER g's `declaration accepted on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            WHEN JUST a  THEN LIST (`Liability` OF a, basis)
        specialUse MEANS
            CONSIDER g's `first breach on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN atAcceptance acceptanceBasis
            WHEN JUST b  THEN
                CONSIDER g's `declaration accepted on`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
                WHEN JUST a  THEN LIST (`Liability` OF a, acceptanceBasis), (`Liability` OF b, `the normal rate, less any earlier liability`)
        acceptanceBasis MEANS
            IF g's `entitled to make the declaration` THEN `the reduced rate for the procedure` ELSE `the applicable rate`

§ `Goal 2 — persons liable`

-- s 6(1) the person in whose name the declaration is made; (2) for s 5
-- liabilities, a person in possession or control on entry; (3) also a person
-- on whose behalf the declaration is made, and others in s 6(3)(b)-(d); (7)
-- "jointly and severally liable".
@ref s 6(1)-(4), (7)
@export The persons jointly and severally liable to import duty under s 6 of the Taxation (Cross-border Trade) Act 2018 (UK): the person in whose name the declaration was made (or, for goods not presented or declared, whoever was in possession or control on entry), the person on whose behalf it was made, and anyone otherwise liable under s 6(3) (a customs agent, or someone involved in a breach knowing or with reason to know of it). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN g IS A `Goods facts`         @desc Whether the goods were declared
      ps IS A LIST OF `Person`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the persons liable for` g `among` ps MEANS
    map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `name`) (filter (GIVEN p YIELD liable p) ps)
    WHERE
        undeclared MEANS
            CONSIDER g's `procedure`
            WHEN `not presented or not declared` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        GIVEN p IS A `Person`
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        liable p MEANS
                (p's `the declaration was made in their name` AND NOT undeclared)
            OR  (p's `in possession or control on entry` AND undeclared)
            OR  p's `the declaration was made on their behalf`
            OR  p's `otherwise liable under s 6(3)`

§ `Goal 3 — amount and notification`

-- s 7, s 16(2): the duty is the applicable rate of the transaction value.
@ref ss 7, 16(2)-(3)
@export The ad valorem import duty under ss 7 and 16 of the Taxation (Cross-border Trade) Act 2018 (UK): the applicable rate (after preferences, quotas, suspensions, remedies and reliefs) applied to the transaction value. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A `Duty facts`  @desc The applicable rate as a percentage and the transaction value
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the import duty for` d MEANS
    d's `rate, percent` DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES d's `transaction value`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

-- Sch 6 para 4 "(1) ... a notification ... must be given before the end of
-- the period of 3 years beginning with the day on which the liability was
-- incurred. (2) If the liability is incurred in circumstances where, in the
-- opinion of an HMRC officer, an offence has been committed ..., the period
-- of 3 years ... is extended to a period of 20 years."
@ref Sch 6 para 4
@export The last day for HMRC to notify a liability to import duty under Schedule 6 para 4 to the Taxation (Cross-border Trade) Act 2018 (UK): the end of the 3 years beginning with the day the liability was incurred, or 20 years where an HMRC officer considers an offence was committed. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN incurred IS A DATE   @desc The day the liability was incurred
      d IS A `Duty facts`  @desc Whether an officer considers an offence was committed
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify a liability incurred on` incurred `with` d MEANS
    IF   d's `an officer thinks an offence was committed`
    THEN `the last day of the` 240 `months beginning with` incurred
    ELSE `the last day of the` 36 `months beginning with` incurred

-- Sch 6 para 1: the liability "may not be enforced unless the person has
-- been notified" in accordance with the Schedule.
@ref Sch 6 paras 1, 4
GIVEN incurred IS A DATE, d IS A `Duty facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a liability incurred on` incurred `is enforceable with` d IF
    CONSIDER d's `notified on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST n  THEN n AT MOST `the last day to notify a liability incurred on` incurred `with` d
